# Requests for the local Web API (started with F5 or `dotnet run --launch-profile https`).
# Visual Studio and VS Code (REST Client) show a "Send request" link above each request.

@Web = https://localhost:7180

### Fetch log - newest first
GET {{Web}}/api/logs?page=1&pageSize=10

### Fetch log - failures for one city
GET {{Web}}/api/logs?city=Rome&status=Failure

### Cities seen so far
GET {{Web}}/api/cities

### Temperature history for a period (ISO 8601 with offset)
GET {{Web}}/api/weather/history?from=2026-10-19T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-20T00:00:00Z

### Invalid: 'from' after 'to' -> 400 problem details
GET {{Web}}/api/weather/history?from=2026-10-20T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-19T00:00:00Z

### Invalid: page size above 200 -> 400 problem details
GET {{Web}}/api/logs?pageSize=500

### Invalid: page above 1000 -> 400 problem details (filter instead of paging that deep)
GET {{Web}}/api/logs?page=1001

### Unknown API route -> 404 problem details (not the SPA)
GET {{Web}}/api/unknown

### Liveness: the process answers (App Service health probe)
GET {{Web}}/health/live

### Readiness: database reachable and a successful fetch within 10 minutes (Degraded otherwise)
GET {{Web}}/health

### OpenAPI document (development only)
GET {{Web}}/openapi/v1.json
